  "system": {
    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p class=\"MsoNormal\">You can keep your catalysts going just for a little longer. When you use a catalyst for a spell that requires you to add an action, you can activate the catalyst early, spending the actions needed. As long as you cast the spell the catalyst was added to by the end of your next turn, the spell benefits from the catalyst. Regardless, the catalyst is expended.</p>"
